 strategic  move of course of course it's a  strategic move and i think russia is  trying to terrorize ukraine to terrorize  ukrainian population uh to force some  concessions from the government for in  kiev and to force ukraine um  to to to move on some some key issues  for russia and of course uh the second  aim i think is to um  to  move ukrainians uh to to become refugees  to leave the country  to block the roads to to maybe um create  difficulties for you of the ukrainian  army and and this is this is what i  think is the goal but it is not working  because ukrainian government is still  fighting and i think it will not give up  it will not yield to russian demands and  even those terrible air strikes that  we've seen for three weeks now um that  they will not um lead for for ukraine to  change its position  roman we don't have much time left but i  wanted to ask you just domestically what  effect this invasion and the  international sanctions are having on  russians  shortly just one example the effect of  sanctions is really growing day by day  and i hear news that russians are really  worried that they will not be having  enough enough um  supplies of  things for their daily needs uh for  example things like pampers for kids  russians are trying to to buy as many as  they can as long there are some steel in  russian shops so we see  spare parts for cars um  some medical equipment some some  medicine  you you name it and there is a huge huge  shortage of such things in russia in the  coming days and weeks i think this is  something russia underestimated  roman goncharenko from dw russian  department thank you very much for the  analysis  two journalists working for the u.s  network fox news have been killed in  ukraine irish cameraman pierre  zakrashevsky seen here at the front of  this photo and ukrainian producer  alexandra kovchinova died when their  vehicle the vehicle they were traveling  in came under fire outside kiev fox news  said another reporter h